From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 18:06:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fonts: Compute FreeType glyph advances without the autohinter

`PlatformFont::glyph_h_advance` loaded every glyph with light hinting to
read its advance. For fonts loaded by FreeType's TrueType driver, light
hinting always runs the autohinter, whose first use on each `FT_Face`
walks the whole character map. Servo creates one face per font size, so
this was paid again for every size, and was 29-56% of layout
instructions on CJK pages on OpenHarmony.

In light mode the autohinter never changes the horizontal scale, so the
advance it produces is the design-unit advance scaled by `x_scale` and
rounded to whole pixels. Compute that directly with `FT_Get_Advance`
whenever a light load would go through the autohinter, and otherwise
keep loading the glyph, now with `FT_LOAD_BITMAP_METRICS_ONLY` so that
color bitmap glyphs are no longer decoded just to be measured.

This intentionally diverges in one case: for a composite glyph with a
`USE_MY_METRICS` component whose advance differs from the composite's
`hmtx` entry, the autohinter uses the component's advance, while the new
code uses `hmtx`. HarfBuzz and other browsers also use the `hmtx` value.
Glyphs whose data FreeType cannot load now also get their `hmtx` advance
instead of none.

Testing: A new unit test checks that the new advance equals the one from
loading the glyph, for every glyph of four TrueType test fonts at eight
sizes, including fractional ones, with and without synthetic bold. It
can be run with `./mach test-unit -p servo-fonts`. Beyond that, a
standalone C program applying the same rule found no difference over
4.7M glyph/size pairs from 159 font faces (system, WPT, test and
HarmonyOS fonts), including variable fonts at several instances with
and without `HVAR`, using both the bundled FreeType 2.13.2 and a system
FreeType 2.14. `css/css-text` and `css/css-fonts` WPT results are
unchanged. On a HarmonyOS phone, layout instructions went down by
27-51% on four pages.

Validation: `./mach test-unit -p servo-fonts` (the new `autohinted_advances_match_loaded_advances` compares every glyph of four TrueType test fonts at eight sizes, with and without synthetic bold, against a glyph load; it fails if the rounding is off by 1/64 px). `./mach test-wpt --release --processes 10 css/css-text css/css-fonts` on upstream main: 2523/2526 expected, the 3 unexpected emoji tests identical with the baseline binary. `servo-freetype-advance-cost/tools/advcheck.c` (same eligibility rule, bundled FreeType 2.13.2 and system 2.14): 0 of 4.7M glyph/size pairs differ. Desktop, 19 sizes of HarmonyOS Sans SC: 1379 -> 1172 M user instructions, screenshots byte-identical. PLR-AL00 production HAP on 357b32533ca, `servoperf page --only load --iterations 5`, two rounds alternating builds, `Layout>::reflow` M instructions/load: chuxing 209.9 -> 102.4, biyadi 205.8 -> 136.6, shibashiji 178.0 -> 118.4, keai-pruned 428.4 -> 312.5; FCP within +-2%.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written and tested by the agent, reviewed by a second agent and the maintainer)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 components/fonts/platform/freetype/font.rs    | 128 +++++++++++++-----
 .../fonts/platform/freetype/freetype_face.rs  |  88 +++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 178 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

